{
 "note": "One world: club crowds, dancers in haze, lasers, neon, DJ decks. Chosen so that consecutive shots belong to the same night.",
 "made_by": {
  "how": "curated",
  "who": "a person looking at a contact sheet of all 55 night-city clips",
  "not": "NOT selected by the system. assets/index.py measures brightness, motion and colour, and none of those separate a club crowd from a star field -- both are dark. The look-cluster duly picked 'dark things': a tape deck, three star fields and a train. Category names were no better: 'dance' contained a man lying on a bed and 'street' a desert highway at sunset. Curating the pool by eye is the honest stand-in for the semantic model this lane does not have, and it is recorded as curation so nobody later reads it as a result.",
  "what_would_replace_it": "An image embedding aligned to text -- CLIP or similar -- so that observations.mood, which is already a text-aligned MUSIC embedding, could select footage in the same space."
 },
